esentations about common technology. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Consonant Blends -- The <span class=\"strong\">sch</span> Sound"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Consonant clusters like /sch/ can occur at the beginning of a word in English. In these words, the /ch/ letters usually sound like /k/. <br/><br/>Practice blending the sound from one consonant sound into the next without adding a vowel sound in between."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the following words aloud."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"*schema\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"school\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"schooled\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"scholar\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"*schedule\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"scheme\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"scholastic\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"schism\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "*The words <span class =\"italic\">schedule</span> and <span class =\"italic\">schema</span> can be pronounced in two ways, like /sk/ or  /sh/.   "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Don't get schooled about eating your vegetables! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Follow these tips and you will create your own schema of healthy eating."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Linking and Deletion with Must  "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When a word ending in consonant +/t/ links into a word beginning with a consonant, the final /t/ of the first word is often deleted. This is often the case with the word <span class =\"italic\">must</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you delete (or drop) the final /t/, the sound before the /t/ must link smoothly into the following word."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You must be starving = You mus_be starving"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When the word <span class =\"italic\">have</span> follows <span class =\"italic\">must</span>,  have is reduced to \u201c_ov\u201d or \u201c_av\u201d.<br/>The 't' sound joins the reduced <span class =\"italic\">have</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "must have   =  mus_tuv or mus_tav "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Phrase</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Pronunciation</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"must find\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"mus_find\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"must be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"mus_be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"must just hustle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"mus_jus_hus_sul\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"must have forgotten\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"mus_tuv forgotten <br/>mus_ta forgotten\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "This is the topic of many articles and conversations, so it must be (mus_be) difficult for many people."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Eating healthy must make (mus_make) a difference in how you feel.  "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to speculate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to guess something, based on what you know already"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I speculate that eating healthy must make a difference in how you feel.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob04aud01"}], "ty